  "description": "EV charging station on the NG9xx platform, Modbus TCP",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-11-10",
  "source": "Alfen ICU B.V., Modbus for ACE, Configuration Guide, version 1.0, 05/2025",
  "sources": [{"title": "Modbus for ACE, Configuration Guide", "version": "1.0", "date": "2025-05", "url": "https://alfen.com/media/1047/download", "note": "Appendices A to F"}],
  "notes": [
    "Every register is a holding register (function 3 to read, 6 and 16 to write). The manual numbers them from 1 and says to subtract 1 for the address on the wire, so the numbers here are 1-based (address_base 1).",
    "Which device answers depends on the Modbus server address: 200 for the station registers (1100 to 1105) and the smart charging network registers (1400 to 1431); 1 for the single socket, or the left socket of a dual socket station; 2 for the right socket. The socket registers (300 to 425 and 1200 to 1215) are read from server address 1 or 2. The manual does not say which address reaches the product identification and date registers (100 to 178). The default unit_id here is 1 (a socket).",
    "32-bit values are mixed-endian: bytes inside a 16-bit word are big-endian and the low word comes first (word_order little). The manual says this only for 32-bit values; the 64-bit values (energy, uptime, meter timestamp) are given the same word order here, which the manual does not state.",
    "A 32-bit value must be read or written in one request, not as two requests. A write to a multi-register value that does not cover all its registers is refused.",
    "A reserved or unavailable register is returned as NaN (0xFFFF for a 16-bit register). Chargers with a Reallin meter made after 2021 return NaN for the sum registers of current, apparent power, reactive power and real energy consumed; older chargers with an ABB meter return numbers.",
    "Strings hold two ASCII characters per register and end with a zero.",
    "Modbus TCP is off by default. It needs the Active Load Balancing licence, and the settings Allow reading, Allow writing maximum currents, Enable sockets and Enable Smart Charging Network must be set in the ACE Service Installer (version 4.0 or later). Up to two clients can connect at the same time. UDP is not supported.",
    "The maximum current registers (1210 and 1417 to 1422) are not kept across a reboot. After the valid time (60 s by default) without a new write the charger falls back to its safe current, so poll more often than the valid time. The safe current must be set before a maximum current can be written.",
    "At most 125 registers can be read in one request.",
    "Register 1104 (OCPP state) is listed as 1104..1105 in the manual, which overlaps 1105 (number of sockets); it is one register here. The meter state bit field (register 300) and meter type (305) values are as listed in the manual. No registers have the firmware, model or serial role because the manual does not say which server address answers the identification registers.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "tcp",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "port": 502,
  "address_base": 1,
  "max_read_registers": 125,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "little",
  "x_status": "official",
